Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Model Response and Interventional Effects for Species Distribution
    Models
Version: 0.13.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Audits model-based environmental responses in species
    distribution modelling. A single raw-unit predictor shift evaluated
    over a fitted model produces a shift effect size and a spatial effect
    map with hard range-masking. Variable selection is a two-stage screen
    whose second stage is a spatial forward search on inner cross-validated
    loss, with no predictor-count cap and no fallback set.
    The effect products carry a hard range diagnostic: rows or cells
    outside the training quantile box are masked, not ranked. This does
    not establish conditional positivity or causal identification. The
    package provides a complete workflow - Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt and
    GAM learners, nested spatial cross-validation, ensemble prediction,
    and future climate projection with extrapolation control. The package
    targets interpretable interventional attribution under stated
    assumptions. Outputs do not establish ecological causality or convert
    presence-background suitability to occurrence probability.
